rows.abstract:
Intends to enhance the enforcement of existing laws regarding counterfeit drugs by increasing the penalty for committing crimes as follows: 
1.mere possession of counterfeit drug;
2.the fake drug is for animals;
3.an act that conceals, substitute, dispose, or destroy any drug as may have been segregated and sealed by the BFAD or who shall break, alter or tamper any mark or seal used by the Bureau to identify those segregated ones;
4.the illness sought to be cured is aggravated or has resulted in physical injury or suffering; and 
5.the counterfeit medicine is the proximate cause of death of a victim who unknowingly purchased and took it.

Proposes to introduce necessary changes as follows:  

1) removal of the 100kW cap to allow more qualified end-users to participate in the program and tasks the ERC to regularly set the maximum kW capacity for distributed generation”¦; 
2) uniform and streamlined permitting process and requirements, and provide minimum requirements for LGUS in accordance with the time frames under the “Energy Virtual One Stop-Shop Act””¦; 
3) a parity pricing methodology that credits end-users the full retail price of the surplus electricity contributed to the electricity grid, including accumulated unused credits from the previous billing period, to correct the double-charging scheme of the current pricing methodology”¦
